/*
  ALL THE CONTENT LIVES HERE.
  To add a new item, copy one line { ... } and change the text.

  l    = level: beginner | intermediate | expert | shortcut | fix | task | forgot
  t    = title (formula name, shortcut keys, or the problem)
  d    = what it does / what to do
  e    = example formula (optional, gets a Copy button)
  a    = answer the example gives (optional)
  alt  = another way if the first way fails (optional)
  tip  = memory trick or extra note (optional)
  cat  = category shown in the Category dropdown (optional)
  u    = how often it is used: daily | sometimes | rare
  v    = Excel version needed: 2013, 2016, 2019, 2021 or 365 (optional)
  k    = hidden search keywords (optional)
  c    = 1 to include it on the printed cheat sheet (optional)

  Examples use the sample sheet shown on the page (SAMPLE below).
  Date examples: A1 = 01/10/2026, B1 = 25/12/2026.
*/

